+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161773 1074 "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](images/65/652258046237288de7102e402a266dd3afff1abfecf97aa2156a351a7611afb3.png) and ![](images/58/58ef5fbadaf595035dc902aac9b66bbce61fea79b6a4144ed060f0486dda982c.png) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 false] [17592186161774 1071 "![](images/4d/4dfdcd2e2f0d80ee8b6633b0dd4bc33b477b22e4db0f2ad36cbfa62eef702659.png)\nConsider the matrix ![](images/15/15fa693fff5bc0eb2a8851089612b5a3fb969c3fd5fbc7c0821e58e52ff4260d.png) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](images/7c/7c7f59284956b7a02d9d9d16387cfba529479fb49aa8efff3bfa908be0fbb04f.png) in terms of the components of ![](images/ed/ed54028979894fad0ac2b928c90c9eeea9361d1c8514fb61ee8ce28435ac2a5c.png) and ![](images/98/9849708035aaa18397dfafbbcdfeb923f576296406c494c30093477f6b2aaa33.png)" 13194139534504 17592186045417 false] [17592186161774 1071 "![](images/75/7505a6fdbe31e7e3e35e1b9b393d04753b0ccd534e5bacda199e8fc902a5fe3c.svg)\nConsider the matrix ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](images/50/50fa4bc1260a734d8f2a1c3045c81dd58e5148d81b6bd85e901c492ab4f61ead.svg) in terms of the components of ![](images/2c/2c28ae197ea4a26ad524d5e6cc89a18a21bf6f215b14432d5377fb3c8a287b6f.svg) and ![](images/35/356a4d35d556458edf899d2b0a49d6db2d47743c0d029c58e1bd3a3b88d9b8c9.svg)" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161774 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](images/b6/b6e5dec69a4614a003b3e1e77d18dfb6747cf556fa6f1374803ab0ffc765a3cb.svg) of ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) corresponds to the term ![](images/6e/6e2dccb072d3420de2a0d2d4c9ad9b3f3ff44f62a59c0b3580ced4cdc42f9c9e.svg) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](images/c3/c3b74ef5a2e970298bd4117c499d18a7bc3319c5e4d4c05b83e0e25fb18fba30.svg)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](images/aa/aa4630ec70bc3741e32a93d26aa15090e187b8e660ce611bc80e20e2bd8114e8.svg)" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161774 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](images/e8/e8f54943816e5af3ad7a3b92ff68887d8126962ffcba1d3109d10390616d8a04.png) of ![](images/33/3397629141c3034fbd4b5cd5bd8c554676175a4b1e3f5eccd26cc5d66ee1bec8.png) corresponds to the term ![](images/e4/e4b6d1207e1c34e37c760af85eb4a4e5594e3db2da2c4ba4841a4106de188c1b.png) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](images/73/734889027df1469d75a4506f295a277b908081224b5860ebf9ec8ea432053dd9.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](images/4c/4ccd64cd17dd595c826e5a8bf13d4bf991c57d128d7a3fbca5a49eaf265f0867.png)" 13194139534504 17592186045417 false] [17592186161775 1074 "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](images/24/24b1e29dccdff51c2ca2c7780a8a5dfcf9c74ed91d48afdde8a14c5127f89ce1.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 false] [17592186161775 1074 "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](images/44/443b1cf1d4425f83b834101627dd202732cf2c905848c8ddbb93dd518f3b35db.svg)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161980 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423356 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161980 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423362 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161981 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423358 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161981 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423361 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161982 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423357 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161982 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423360 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161983 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423355 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186161983 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423359 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186162217 1050 540.0 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186162590 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186162590 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186162590 1071 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form $x^{T}Ay$ in terms of the components of $x = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $y = \\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$?" 13194139534504 17592186045417 false] [17592186162590 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186163225 1064 "Let $n$ be a positive integer. A  function \n\n$$\nf: \\Bbb R^n \\to \\Bbb R\n$$\n\nis a **linear form**  (or  *linear functional*) if there is a row-vector \n\n![](images/95/952d8832a903cf184286698e449da84d94d61cb46d984a48f33f406a42a8007a.svg)\n\nsuch that for any ![](images/6b/6b756f37311a5e7f4e6cfb160a37b31d54b2ce1e29849044101dc82d49e44d21.svg) we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={a}_{1}{x}_{1}+{a}_{2}{x}_{2}+…+{a}_{n}{x}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let $f(\\mathbf{x})$ be the linear form   defined on $\\Bbb R^2$ by $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](images/26/26cf6eb0836041b648c29908c8d13ae132e644ea68c772e81e011470283c3427.svg) \n\nSuppose we want to evaluate $f(\\mathbf{x})$ at ![](images/5d/5d6ebda5e8563d23b66cdf15f4a47a1ae712510eeacbe6bcebd031534bcc841a.svg) Then, we simply substitute ![](images/6c/6c79170289a47e3ebb2a7226432938640c63ccea0d032e674d4f03967c12c8ea.svg) and obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186163225 1064 "Let $n$ be a positive integer. A  function \n\n$$\nf: \\Bbb R^n \\to \\Bbb R\n$$\n\nis a **linear form**  (or  *linear functional*) if there is a row-vector \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that for any $[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={a}_{1}{x}_{1}+{a}_{2}{x}_{2}+…+{a}_{n}{x}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let $f(\\mathbf{x})$ be the linear form   defined on $\\Bbb R^2$ by $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where $[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ \n\nSuppose we want to evaluate $f(\\mathbf{x})$ at $[\\begin{aligned}\\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}]$ Then, we simply substitute $[\\begin{aligned}\\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}]$ and obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,1 \\\\ \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 false] [17592186163234 1064 "Let $n$ be a positive integer. A  function $B: \\Bbb R^n\\times \\Bbb R^n \\to \\Bbb R$ is said to be a **bilinear form** if there is an $n\\times n$   matrix $A$ such that \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}) =  \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A\\mathbf{y}, \\qquad  \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\in \\Bbb R^n.\n$$\n\nSuppose, fo