077 "selection" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423353 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423334 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423353 1079 #uuid "d1fd5e82-7e1e-5e80-89d9-fc63ac2ef995" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423312 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423321 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423325 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423326 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423331 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1077 "selection" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423331 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423354 1079 #uuid "e18439f9-3a62-5bbd-b03d-810c0b754554" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423355 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423352 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423355 1069 "q-94050" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423355 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423355 1071 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423355 1072 #uuid "41f16b5c-e680-54f8-926b-ebe6345d8561" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423355 1074 "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+1=0.\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423356 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423347 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423356 1069 "q-93906" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423356 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423356 1071 "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423356 1072 #uuid "6cffcafb-88aa-554a-9e0e-d0b676da85d1" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423356 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10-8-3+4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423357 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423349 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423357 1069 "q-93997" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423357 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423357 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423357 1072 #uuid "8f253585-3e9e-576c-84e8-68a00302ab3a" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423357 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-5){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-5{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-2{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423358 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423353 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423358 1069 "q-93979" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423358 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423358 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423358 1072 #uuid "8fd187ae-a269-5381-90d7-f0ba2d5b4ded" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423358 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423359 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423351 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423359 1069 "q-140864" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423359 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423359 1071 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & b & -2 \\\\ c & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b-c?$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423359 1072 #uuid "a33de8e7-0315-5081-b30e-a76239172d51" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423359 1074 "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b-c=3+(-5)-(-2)=0.\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423360 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423348 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423360 1069 "q-93991" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423360 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423360 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423360 1072 #uuid "b15d4431-e43f-5101-96e7-ab09f0076b4a" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423360 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423361 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423350 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423361 1069 "q-93920" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423361 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423361 1071 "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423361 1072 #uuid "bc56657a-b79e-53ee-87cf-34f486cb39d6" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423361 1074 "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}. \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-0+0-1-2 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423362 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423354 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423362 1069 "q-93972" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423362 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423362 1071 "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423362 1072 #uuid "d2074d50-adbe-5509-b588-3fcd898ef1ff" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true] [17592186423362 1074 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 5+4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =4+15-12 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534504 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-08e5bf9a-2ab7-5739-b14d-f546e211c130" 17592186423302 "answer-09004ef9-4917-58d2-8c07-5742c23a3707" 17592186423303 "answer-0b02a7dc-3d77-54f9-9eab-4104398fd87b" 17592186423304 "answer-16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" 17592186423305 "answer-1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" 17592186423306 "answer-21bd4957-61ca-515f-955c-429ec430a2c2" 17592186423307 "answer-22b8fa47-b5d7-5475-809f-5b86289a33ef" 1759